                "text": "{\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"missing_hyp\",\n      \"location\": \"(hcodd : ∀ n : ℕ, n > 0 → c (2 * n + 1) = (-1) ^ n * c n)\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The informal rules include c(2n)=c(n), but the Lean hypotheses do not. The proposition therefore ranges over functions whose even-indexed values are unrestricted.\",\n      \"prediction\": \"The negation should be provable: start with a function satisfying the informal recurrences and change only c(2014). The odd recurrence can still be satisfied by updating its later descendants. The summand at n=2012 changes because c(2012) is nonzero, while no other summand in the stated range changes. Thus both resulting sums cannot equal the fixed answer.\",\n      \"probe_kind\": \"negated_statement\",\n      \"comparison\": null,\n      \"witnesses\": null,\n      \"edit_from\": null,\n      \"edit_to\": null,\n      \"bridge\": \"intrinsic\",\n      \"obligation\": \"Construct the functions and verify the odd recurrence and finite-sum difference in Lean; this is a suspected omission, not a confirmed counterexample.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The formal proposition omits the recurrence for even indices.\"\n}"
